module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.mirror_population_exceeds_install_ownership

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data mirror_population_exceeds_install_ownership: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "mirror_population_exceeds_install_ownership" as NonEmptyStr,
  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: regeneration produces a module mirror but the installer's package-ownership join omits its owner. HARM: emission and adjudication succeed, then RebuildScopeRefused MirrorHasNoOwningPackage stops the build and restores the installation checkpoint. Taking the candidate by hand bypasses the broken transaction and conceals the missing join; the refusal is correct, the incomplete ownership population is the defect.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: the compared mirror population, module-bearing partition rows, and executable shell declarations are different populations. A partition-only join cannot describe a module compiled directly by the shell. Absence from a partition must not imply shell ownership: the shell declaration must positively match, and a match in both populations must refuse MirrorHasMultipleOwningPackages. Aggregate and release-excluded products have separately modeled roles rather than fabricated module owners.",
    "HISTORICAL RECEIPTS moved from CONTROL 4 in src/v2/test/claim/stage0_partition_rebuild_scope_witness_test.dag: cli_run.rs was a real hand-authored host module without a partition owner. The generated v1_compiler_compiler_tests_rust.rs refused on 2026-09-02; #10037 gave it its v1-infer partition owner. The generated v1_compiler_infer_resolve.rs refused on 2026-09-09 and received its v1-infer owner. The two partition repairs remain asserted by witness_compiler_tests_rust_rebuild_owner_is_v1_infer_holds and witness_infer_resolve_rebuild_owner_is_v1_infer_holds. The hand-authored instance alone did not establish the generated-output gap; the generated instances did.",
    "SHELL INSTANCE: bright-bear-236 reported v1_compiler_compile.rs on #11072 and valiant-badger-803 encountered it again. #9777 introduced HostShellEmittedOwner in v2.compiler.self_host.stage0_executable_assembly, while rebuild_scope_owners_of_mirror still read only partition rows. This is an omitted derived ownership arm, not a renamed file or one missing hand-authored roster row. v1.compiler.emit_rust emit_lib_rs_from_paths already derives the shell declarations from emitted modules outside module-bearing partitions.",
    "REPRODUCTION for #11094: current main 011877f603, with only a controlled stale comment in the generated compile mirror, executed and adjudicated all 155 planned mirrors, then exited 1: StageSeedBuildRefused: no partitioned build was attempted and no full-build fallback ran -- partition-rebuild: RebuildScopeRefused MirrorHasNoOwningPackage mirror=v1_compiler_compile.rs. The driver reported checkpoint restored. The clean baseline d9cc353 had no drift and therefore did not exercise installation.",
    "REPAIR AND EXECUTED WITNESSES: #11094 threads the observed shell declarations through the modeled ownership decision and round-cost receipt, reusing the convergence manifest reader. The model witnesses exercise shell ownership, removed-owner refusal, and shell/partition duplicate refusal. The native live_module_mirrors_have_owners_and_removed_shell_owner_refuses test at 345c50ba joined every emitted module identity independently against the package map, then removed the compile shell declaration and obtained the exact named refusal. Its module population excludes products through the independent generation-role authority, never through presence in the ownership map.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: 1 (mitigatable), because the typed installation refusal and rollback contain the harm after expensive regeneration. CEILING: 2 (mechanically preventable) for the live module-population coverage obligation, because an independent identity join can decide it. That witness executes locally, but the merge-path coverage remains at rung 1: cargo test --lib is not on the required CI path (the pre-existing gunbc.rung_drop.rust_unit_tests_off_the_merge_path). The controlled .dag witnesses run on that path but do not establish live population completeness. The installed shell observation is still a host read, so this row does not claim ownership completeness is unrepresentable by construction.",
    "NEXT TRIGGER: make the independent emitted-module-population versus positive package-map identity join a required consumer before installation, with the existing removed-owner mutation proving its named refusal. Preserve the positive ownership arms and duplicate refusal; neither filtering the subject population through the map nor defaulting every unowned mirror to the shell closes the class."
  ],
  evidence: [],
}
